  "question": {
    "text": "A solid has a ' $b c c$ ' structure. If the distance of nearest approach between two atoms is $1.73 Å$, the edge length of the cell is",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "6ZTVc",
      "text": "\n$314.20 \\mathrm{pm}$\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "7pvK5",
      "text": "\n$1.41 \\mathrm{pm}$\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "nGidm",
      "text": "\n$200 \\mathrm{pm}$\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": true
    },
    {
      "id": "aiqCW",
      "text": "\n$216 \\mathrm{pm}$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "For bcc structure\n$$\nd=\\frac{\\sqrt{3} a}{2}\n$$\nwhere $d=$ distance between two atoms $a=$ edge length\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n& 1.73=\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2} a \\\\\n& a=\\frac{2 \\times 1.73}{\\sqrt{3}}=2 Å=200 \\mathrm{pm}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$",
    "image": null
  },
